{{!-- GM MOVES — the playbook's first spread: the basic list, then Exploration, then Homefront.
      Reference only. Nothing here rolls and nothing here is stored; the lists come from
      module/gm-toolkit/gm-moves.js.

      `class="tab moves"` is load-bearing, not a copy-paste leftover, though NOT for the
      reason the same class carries elsewhere. What it earns is the tab's padding, the 14px gap
      between move groups, and the fold caret's box — all three written against `.tab.moves`
      plus `.stonetop-move-group`. Nothing unwanted rides along: the learned-move filter is
      `.tab.moves.hide-unselected`, and only the character sheet ever adds that class.

      The ENTRIES are deliberately not the bordered move card, and they say so by wearing their
      own classes rather than the shared card's. They used to carry `stonetop-item` and its
      three children and the stylesheet took the card back off again declaration by
      declaration; a reference entry shares nothing with a card but its font, so it is cheaper
      to describe than to undo.

      `data-tab="moves"` is also what earns the rail's move glyph — the icon table in
      stonetop.css is one flat list keyed by data-tab, with no per-sheet scope.

      Each section is BOXED in its own `.stonetop-move-group`. The fold walk claims a heading's
      following siblings until it meets the next heading (utils/section-editing.js), so three
      headings in one flat run would let the Basic caret swallow Exploration and Homefront. --}}
<div class="tab moves" data-group="primary" data-tab="moves">
	<section class="sheet-tab stonetop-gm-toolkit-moves">

		{{#each stonetop.moveSections}}
		<div class="stonetop-move-group">
			{{!-- The tab's own name lives in a tooltip now that the rail is icon-only, so these
			      headings are the only place the page says what it is.

			      `randomize` is the die beside the note: it draws one move out of THIS section
			      and whispers it to the GM (module/gm-toolkit/random-gm-move.js). Keyed by the
			      section's own key, so the three buttons need no wiring of their own. --}}
			{{> "stonetop.section-heading" title=title note=note collapse=collapseId
			                              randomize=key randomizeTitle=randomizeTitle}}
			<ol class="items-list">
				{{#each moves}}
				<li class="stonetop-gm-move">
					<strong class="stonetop-gm-move-name">{{name}}</strong>
					{{#if gloss}}<div class="stonetop-gm-move-gloss">{{gloss}}</div>{{/if}}
				</li>
				{{/each}}
			</ol>
		</div>
		{{/each}}

	</section>
</div>
